  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.705pt, 804.24pt, "14 ")
  #line-at(80.88pt, 68.16pt, "In conclusion, this study presents a comprehensive analysis of the depth-dependent thermal ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 95.76pt, "conductivity profile of an HFCVD diamond film on a SiC substrate, along with the quantification of ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 123.36pt, "key interfacial thermal resistances. Using the frequency-dependent SPS thermoreflectance technique, ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 150.96pt, "we observed that the effective thermal conductivity increases monotonically from the nucleation ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 178.56pt, "interface to the growth surface, a trend that correlates with grain coarsening observed via EBSD. This ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 206.16pt, "approach also enabled the simultaneous determination of the diamond/substrate interfacial ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 233.76pt, "conductance, a parameter typically inaccessible to higher-frequency techniques.  ")
  #line-at(80.88pt, 261.36pt, "The methodology established herein provides a robust framework for characterizing anisotropic ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 288.96pt, "and heterogeneous material systems, which is crucial for optimizing thermal management in next-")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 316.56pt, "generation high-power electronic devices. While the exponential model offers a good fit to the ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 344.16pt, "experimental data, it assumes a uniform grain size evolution across the entire film, which may not ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 371.76pt, "hold in films with significant impurities or defects. Future work incorporating more complex models ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 399.36pt, "or higher-order terms could further refine our understanding of thermal conductivity in ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 426.96pt, "polycrystalline films and inform the design of advanced thermal management materials. ")
  #line-at(80.88pt, 454.56pt, "See the Supplementary Material for details of the optimization of HFCVD processes, derivation ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 482.16pt, "of the weighted harmonic mean model, input parameters, measured signals at all modulation ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 509.76pt, "frequencies, uncertainty analysis, evaluation of alternative models, and the MATLAB code used for ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 537.36pt, "the numerical calculations. ")
  #line-at(80.88pt, 592.56pt, "X.Q. acknowledges the funding support from National Key R&D program (2022YFA1203100). ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 620.16pt, "J.W. acknowledges support from the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC) through ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 647.76pt, "Grant No. 52172037 and the Natural Science Foundation of Beijing through Grant No. L259007. P.J. ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 675.36pt, "acknowledges support from the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC) through Grant ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 702.96pt, "No. 52376058. ")
